<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mughal war of succession (1657–1661)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1657">1657</a>–<a href="/years/1661">1661</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Mughal war of succession (1658–1659)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mughal war of succession broke out when the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> fell ill in 1657 and his four sons fought for the throne. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>, allied at first with Murad Bakhsh, defeated his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dara-shikoh">Dara Shikoh</a> at Samugarh in 1658, imprisoned his father and was crowned. Dara was captured and executed in 1659, Shah Shuja fled to Arakan, and Murad was executed in 1661.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mughal-war-of-succession-1657-1661.jpg" alt="Mughal war of succession (1657–1661)" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Payag · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Samugarh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
